      "message": "Many of the usages simply pass a `byte []` that has already been calculated, only `RevCommit::parseHeaders` and `RevWalk::parseNew` actually defer something, but you could rewrite the 1st like this:\n\n```java\n@Override\nfinal void parseHeaders(RevWalk walk) throws MissingObjectException, IncorrectObjectTypeException, IOException {\n\tif (graphPosition \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 !walk.isRetainBody()) {\n\t\tparseCanonical(walk, null);\n\t} else {\n\t\tparseCanonical(walk, walk.getCachedBytes(this));\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n... and the 2nd one doesn\u0027t seem to be that expensive since both of its callers already did an `open(...)` operation, which I bet is the one that reads from disk, right?\n\nDo you have any performance measurements that can support the need for this change?",
